      "patch": "@@ -1,7 +1,16 @@\n-Thank you for your interest in the paper and the code. I am currently quite occupied with other commitments.\n+# A baseline example of wind field reconstruction using nacelle lidar measurement and physics-informed neural network\n+# Feng Guo @ Shanghai Jiao Tong University  3 Feb. 2026\n+# This method is presented in the Paper:\n+# On Wind Directions Estimated by Nacelle Lidar UnderDifferent Reconstruction Methods, Wind Energy\n+# https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1002/we.70098\n \n-I will organize the code and add comments where necessary to improve readability. I expect to publish the initial release within the next 10 days.\n+# Note: This code is intended for demonstration purposes only.\n+# It has been tested only for the non-yawed case and does not account for sequential lidar scanning. \n \n-Best regards,\n-Feng Guo\n+# Please install the dependenies in the requirements.txt first.\n+\n+# Hope this code is helpful for your investigation.\n+# Please cite this paper if you find this code helpful for your research.\n+\n+Author: Feng Guo\n fengguo@sjtu.edu.cn"
